{
  "locale": "ko",
  "version": 4,
  "_comment": [
    "Phrasing templates for the Announcements feature. See dev/announcements.md §3.",
    "Each bucket has a `balanced` list (always present, used by Balanced verbosity)",
    "and an optional `chatty` list (longer / more conversational variants used when",
    "the user picks Chatty). Minimal verbosity bypasses these templates and speaks",
    "just `{name}.` directly. Translators rewrite natively, not literally.",
    "",
    "Korean notes:",
    "  - Particle trap: Korean particles change with the final consonant of the",
    "    preceding word (이/가, 은/는, 을/를, 와/과, 으로/로, 이에요/예요), and",
    "    {name} is unknown at speak time. Never attach those particles directly to",
    "    {name}. Safe forms after {name}: a space, punctuation, 입니다, 인, 일,",
    "    같아요, 에, 도, 하고, or a following noun such as 소리.",
    "  - No counters (마리 etc.) and no word for 'bird' (새): the model also covers",
    "    insects, amphibians and mammals. Use 종 when a noun is needed.",
    "  - Register: polite 해요체 (존댓말), consistent with the polite ARB strings.",
    "  - Punctuation: periods, commas and question marks only, for natural TTS pauses."
  ],
